px; background: rgba(53,163,204,.35); }\n  .pipe-col.three { right: 7px; }\n  .node {\n    display: inline-block;\n    border: 1px solid #777;\n    background: white;\n    padding: 4px 5px;\n    margin: 2px;\n    min-width: 41px;\n  }\n  .oval {\n    display: block;\n    width: 72px;\n    border: 1px solid #777;\n    border-radius: 50%;\n    padding: 5px 1px;\n    margin: 10px auto 11px;\n    background: white;\n  }\n  .pipe-line {\n    position: absolute;\n    width: 1px;\n    height: 53px;\n    background: #777;\n    top: 41px;\n    left: 55px;\n  }\n  figcaption {\n    font-size: 12.5px;\n    line-height: 1.17;\n    margin-top: 7px;\n  }\n  .tree-diagram {\n    height: 220px;\n    margin-top: 3px;\n    border-left: 1px solid #444;\n    border-bottom: 1px solid #444;\n    position: relative;\n    background:\n      linear-gradient(to bottom, transparent 24%, #777 24.3%, transparent 24.7%),\n      linear-gradient(to bottom, transparent 49%, #777 49.3%, transparent 49.7%),\n      linear-gradient(to bottom, transparent 74%, #777 74.3%, transparent 74.7%),\n      linear-gradient(to right, transparent 24%, #777 24.3%, transparent 24.7%),\n      linear-gradient(to right, transparent 49%, #777 49.3%, transparent 49.7%),\n      linear-gradient(to right, transparent 74%, #777 74.3%, transparent 74.7%);\n  }\n  .tree-diagram .time {\n    position: absolute;\n    left: -10px;\n    top: 91px;\n    transform: rotate(-90deg);\n    font-size: 10px;\n  }\n  .tree-diagram .label {\n    position: absolute;\n    font-size: 10px;\n    background: rgba(255,255,255,.75);\n    padding: 1px 2px;\n  }\n  .branches {\n    position: absolute;\n    left: 32px;\n    right: 20px;\n    top: 18px;\n    bottom: 22px;\n  }\n  .branch {\n    position: absolute;\n    height: 2px;\n    background: #786652;\n    transform-origin: left center;\n  }\n  .b1 { width: 145px; left: 0; top: 145px; transform: rotate(-48deg); }\n  .b2 { width: 150px; left: 105px; top: 34px; transform: rotate(45deg); }\n  .b3 { width: 122px; left: 0; top: 145px; transform: rotate(18deg); }\n  .b4 { width: 135px; left: 114px; top: 180px; transform: rotate(-25deg); }\n  .b5 { width: 100px; left: 218px; top: 110px; transform: rotate(25deg); }\n  .tips {\n    position: absolute;\n    left: 18px;\n    right: 12px;\n    bottom: 4px;\n    height: 34px;\n    background: repeating-linear-gradient(90deg,#39a6a4 0 2px,transparent 2px 6px,#d33 6px 8px,transparent 8px 12px);\n    opacity: .75;\n  }\n  .operator-intro {\n    min-height: 50px;\n    border-top: 1px solid #4a7f94;\n    padding: 27px 4px 8px;\n    font-size: 14px;\n    white-space: nowrap;\n  }\n  .operators {\n    display: grid;\n    grid-template-columns: 1.05fr 1fr 1.15fr 1fr 1.12fr 91px;\n    align-items: stretch;\n    height: 76px;\n    margin-bottom: 10px;\n  }\n  .operator {\n    display: flex;\n    align-items: center;\n    justify-content: center;\n    padding: 4px 8px;\n    border-right: 1px solid #7fa1ad;\n    text-align: center;\n    font-size: 14px;\n    line-height: 1.15;\n    font-weight: bold;\n  }\n  .operator:last-of-type { border-right: 0; }\n  .arrow {\n    align-self: center;\n    height: 66px;\n    color: white;\n    background: #559fd2;\n    clip-path: polygon(0 34%,100% 0,100% 100%,0 66%,20% 50%);\n    display: flex;\n    align-items: center;\n    justify-content: flex-end;\n    padding-right: 5px;\n    font-size: 13px;\n    font-weight: bold;\n  }\n  .right-column .section-title { margin-bottom: 5px; }\n  .charts {\n    display: grid;\n    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);\n    column-gap: 22px;\n    row-gap: 20px;\n    padding: 0 13px 0 25px;\n  }\n  .chart {\n    height: 178px;\n    text-align: center;\n    font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;\n    font-size: 9px;\n  }\n  .chart-title {\n    font-size: 10px;\n    font-weight: bold;\n    letter-spacing: .3px;\n    height: 29px;\n    line-height: 1.2;\n  }\n  .plot {\n    width: 170px;\n    height: 113px;\n    margin: 0 auto;\n    position: relative;\n    border-left: 1px solid #333;\n    border-bottom: 1px solid #333;\n    background:\n      linear-gradient(145deg, transparent 49.2%, #777 49.5%, #777 50%, transparent 50.3%);\n  }\n  .plot::before {\n    content: \"Posterior\\A estimate\";\n    white-space: pre;\n    position: absolute;\n    left: -45px;\n    top: 36px;\n    transform: rotate(-90deg);\n    line-height: 10px;\n  }\n  .plot::after {\n    content: \"\";\n    position: absolute;\n    left: 8px;\n    bottom: 6px;\n    width: 67px;\n    height: 32px;\n    background:\n      radial-gradient(circle at 10% 80%, #000 0 1.4px, transparent 1.8px),\n      radial-gradient(circle at 18% 66%, #159ab0 0 1.4px, transparent 1.8px),\n      radial-gradient(circle at 27% 72%, #000 0 1.4px, transparent 1.8px),\n      radial-gradient(circle at 34% 54%, #128aa1 0 1.4px, transparent 1.8px),\n      radial-gradient(circle at 43% 64%, #000 0 1.4px, transparent 1.8px),\n      radial-gradient(circle at 52% 42%, #159ab0 0 1.4px, transparent 1.8px),\n      radial-gradient(circle at 62% 47%, #000 0 1.4px, transparent 1.8px),\n      radial-gradient(circle at 75% 25%, #148fa7 0 1.4px, transparent 1.8px),\n      radial-gradient(circle at 88% 34%, #000 0 1.4px, transparent 1.8px);\n  }\n  .chart:nth-child(2) .plot::after,\n  .chart:nth-child(5) .plot::after,\n  .chart:nth-child(11) .plot::after {\n    width: 67px; height: 45px; left: 31px; bottom: 29px;\n    background: repeating-linear-gradient(90deg,rgba(0,148,180,.75) 0 2px,transparent 2px 4px);\n  }\n  .chart:nth-child(6) .plot::after { left: 4px; bottom: 4px; height: 70px; }\n  .chart:nth-child(7) .plot::after { width: 82px; height: 45px; }\n  .chart:nth-child(8) .plot::after { width: 76px; height: 25px; }\n  .chart:nth-child(9) .plot::after { width: 98px; height: 49px; }\n  .axis-label { margin-top: 5px; font-size: 9px; }\n  .results-note {\n    margin: 2px 6px 8px;\n    font-size: 13.5px;\n    line-height: 1.17;\n    text-align: center;\n  }\n  .conclusion {\n    margin-top: 3px !important;\n    margin-bottom: 3px !important;\n  }\n  .conclusion-text {\n    margin: 0 12px 5px;\n    font-size: 13.5px;\n    line-height: 1.2;\n    text-align: center;\n  }\n  .footer {\n    border-top: 1px solid #777;\n    display: grid;\n    grid-template-columns: 1fr 120px;\n    column-gap: 8px;\n    padding-top: 3px;\n  }\n  .footer-text {\n    font-size: 12.5px;\n    line-height: 1.16;\n  }\n  .footer-text p { margin: 0 0 4px; }\n  .qr-title {\n    text-align: center;\n    font-size: 14px;\n    font-weight: bold;\n    line-height: 1.2;\n  }\n  .qr {\n    width: 108px;\n    height: 108px;\n    margin: 3px auto 0;\n    border: 4px solid #111;\n    background:\n      linear-gradient(90deg, #111 12%, transparent 12% 20%, #111 20% 28%, transparent 28% 39%, #111 39% 46%, transparent 46% 55%, #111 55% 65%, transparent 65% 73%, #111 73% 84%, transparent 84%),\n      linear-gradient(#111 10%, transparent 10% 19%, #111 19% 27%, transparent 27% 37%, #111 37% 46%, transparent 46% 57%, #111 57% 67%, transparent 67% 76%, #111 76% 87%, transparent 87%);\n    image-rendering: pixelated;\n  }\n  sup { font-size: 60%; }\n</style>\n</head>\n<body>\n<main class=\"poster\">\n  <h1 class=\"main-title\">WELL CALIBRATED SIMULATION STUDY OF A NOVEL ADAPTIVE<br>\n  PARALLELISED BAYESIAN INFERENCE OF THE MULTISPECIES COALESCENT<br>\n  MODEL TESTING A DIFFERENT NUMBER OF TAXA AND GENES.</h1>\n\n  <header class=\"identity\">\n    <div class=\"auckland-logo\">\n      <div class=\"crest\"><strong>✧</strong>[Crest]</div>\n      <div class=\"uni-name\">\n        <div class=\"small\">THE UNIVERSITY OF</div>\n        <div class=\"large\">AUCKLAND</div>\n        <div class=\"maori\">Te Whare Wānanga o Tāmaki Makaurau</div>\n        <div class=\"nz\">NEW ZEALAND</div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n\n    <div class=\"authors\">\n      <div class=\"names\">Hu Ge<sup>1</sup>, Jordan Douglas<sup>2</sup>, Remco Bouckaert<sup>2</sup></div>\n      <div>(1) School of Biological Sciences, University of Auckland, Auckland 1010, New Zealand</div>\n      <div>(2) School of Computer Science, University of Auckland, Auckland, 1010, New Zealand</div>\n    </div>\n\n    <div class=\"beast\">\n      <div class=\"mouse placeholder\">[Mouse logo]</div>\n      Beast2\n    </div>\n  </header>\n\n  <div class=\"content\">\n    <section class=\"left-column\">\n      <h2 class=\"section-title\">Introduction</h2>\n      <p>A novel Parallelised Bayesian Inference of the Multispecies Coalescent with new MCMC proposals has been implemented in the open-source BEAST 2 platform as the StarBeast3 package. This new approach avoids biases, such as being an inconsistent estimator of the tree topology. Furthermore, it explores the state space much more efficiently, allowing the handle of data sets one and a half orders of magnitude larger than StarBeast2 and more than two orders faster than *BEAST.</p>\n\n      <p><strong>Our goal</strong> was to establish the correct implementation of StarBeast3 by testing different numbers of taxa and genes.</p>\n\n      <p class=\"keywords\"><strong>Key words:</strong> multispecies coalescent; BEAST 2; phylogenetics;<br>\n      bayesian inference; high performance; adaptive; parallelisation.</p>\n\n      <h2 class=\"section-title methods\">Methods</h2>\n      <p>We performed well calibration studies by simulating alignments using parameters directly sampled from the prior distribution, and then we inferred the posterior estimates of these parameters using StarBeast3 <strong>(Figure 1).</strong></p>\n\n      <figure class=\"figure\">\n        <div class=\"pipeline placeholder\">\n          <div class=\"pipe-col one\">\n            <span class=\"node\">prior.xml</span>\n            <span class=\"oval\">1. BEAST</span>\n            <span class=\"node\">true.log</span>\n            <span class=\"node\">XML template</span>\n            <span class=\"node\">true.log</span>\n            <span class=\"oval\">2. CoverageTestXMLGenerator</span>\n            <div class=\"pipe-line\"></div>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"pipe-col two\">\n            <span class=\"node\">beast.xml</span>\n            <span class=\"oval\">3. BEAST</span>\n            <span class=\"node\">trace.log</span>\n            <span class=\"node\">tree.log</span>\n            <span class=\"oval\">4. loganalyser</span>\n            <div>N times</div>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"pipe-col three\">\n            <span class=\"node\">summary</span>\n            <span class=\"oval\">5. CoverageCalculator</span>\n            <span class=\"node\">coverage stats</span>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n        <figcaption><strong>Figure 1.</strong> Pipeline of 5 steps implemented by Experimenter package in BEAST 2 that assists in simulation studies to verify correctness of the implementation. (1) Set up XML for desired model and sample from prior. (2) Generate (MCMC) analysis for each of the samples (support for multiple alignments). (3) Run the analyses using StarBeast3 package in BEAST2. (4) Use loganalyser to summarise trace files. (5) Run CoverageCalculator to summarise coverage of parameters. <strong>Source:</strong> <em>https://github.com/rbouckaert/DeveloperManual.git</em></figcaption>\n      </figure>\n\n      <p>We evaluated a strict and relaxed clock model, across varying tree sizes ( 4 species: 12 taxa; 16 species: 48 taxa), and multiple genes (10, 50, 100, and 200). With 100 independent runs, we estimated the coverage of the true value by the 95% highest probability density (HPD) estimates for various parameters in the model <strong>(Figure 2)</strong> and its newly developed efficient MCMC operators.</p>\n\n      <figure class=\"figure\">\n        <div class=\"tree-diagram placeholder\">\n          <span class=\"time\">Time</span>\n          <div class=\"branches\">\n            <span class=\"branch b1\"></span><span class=\"branch b2\"></span>\n            <span class=\"branch b3\"></span><span class=\"branch b4\"></span>\n            <span class=\"branch b5\"></span>\n          </div>\n          <span class=\"label\" style=\"top:5px;left:25px;\">Branchrates<br>r1, ..., r<sub>k-1</sub><br>(optional)</span>\n          <span class=\"label\" style=\"top:1px;left:123px;\">Relative clock<br>rates v1, ..., v<sub>k</sub></span>\n          <span class=\"label\" style=\"top:34px;left:202px;\">Species tree S</span>\n          <span class=\"label\" style=\"top:66px;left:265px;\">Site models v1, ..., v<sub>k</sub></span>\n          <span class=\"label\" style=\"top:116px;left:251px;\">Gene trees g1, ..., g<sub>k</sub></span>\n          <span class=\"label\" style=\"top:137px;left:80px;\">Population sizes<br>Ne1, ..., Ne2n-1</span>\n          <div class=\"tips\"></div>\n          <span class=\"label\" style=\"bottom:0;left:79px;\">Alignments D1, ... ,Dk</span>\n        </div>\n        <figcaption><strong>Figure 2.</strong> Simulated species trees S with n = 16 species with k = 100 gene trees embedded. Parameters in the multispecies coalescent model are indicated in the figure: Node heights (time) are shown on the y-axis, and effective population sizes are on the x-axis. Species tree branch rates are indicated by line thickness. Colors show Gen trees. The tree was built from a Direct simulator in BEAST2 and visualized using UglyTrees (Douglas, 2020).</figcaption>\n      </figure>\n    </section>\n\n    <section class=\"right-column\">\n      <div class=\"operator-intro\"><strong>Novel MCMC operators</strong> which generate proposals that explore the state space more efficiently implementing in Starbeast3:</div>\n\n      <div class=\"operators\">\n        <div class=\"operator\">Effective<br>Population Size<br>Gibbs Operator</div>\n        <div class=\"operator\">Bactrian<br>Operators for<br>Trees</div>\n        <div class=\"operator\">Adaptive variance<br>multivariate<br>normal (AVMN)<br>operator</div>\n        <div class=\"operator\">Parallel Gene Tree<br>Operator</div>\n        <div class=\"operator\">Species Tree<br>Relaxed Clock<br>Model Operators</div>\n        <div class=\"arrow\">StarBeast3</div>\n      </div>\n\n      <h2 class=\"section-title\">Results</h2>\n\n      <div class=\"charts\">\n        <div class=\"chart\">\n          <div class=\"chart-title\">Species tree height<br><span style=\"font-weight:normal\">Coverage: 96%</span></div>\n          <div class=\"plot\"></div><div class=\"axis-label\">True value</div>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"chart\">\n          <div class=\"chart-title\">Species tree birth rate<br><span style=\"font-weight:normal\">Coverage: 94%</span></div>\n          <div class=\"plot\"></div><div class=\"axis-label\">True value</div>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"chart\">\n          <div class=\"chart-title\">Gene tree height<br><span style=\"font-weight:normal\">Coverage: 91%</span></div>\n          <div class=\"plot\"></div><div class=\"axis-label\">True value</div>\n        </div>\n\n        <div class=\"chart\">\n          <div class=\"chart-title\">Clock model standard deviation<br><span style=\"font-weight:normal\">Coverage: 97%</span></div>\n          <div class=\"plot\"></div><div class=\"axis-label\">True value</div>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"chart\">\n          <div class=\"chart-title\">Branch rate mean<br><span style=\"font-weight:normal\">Coverage: 92%</span></div>\n          <div class=\"plot\"></div><div class=\"axis-label\">True value</div>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"chart\">\n          <div class=\"chart-title\">Branch rate variance<br><span style=\"font-weight:normal\">Coverage: 97%</span></div>\n          <div class=\"plot\"></div><div class=\"axis-label\">True value</div>\n        </div>\n\n        <div class=\"chart\">\n          <div class=\"chart-title\">Transition-transversion ratio<br><span style=\"font-weight:normal\">Coverage: 96%</span></div>\n          <div class=\"plot\"></div><div class=\"axis-label\">True value</div>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"chart\">\n          <div class=\"chart-title\">Gene tree substitution rate<br><span style=\"font-weight:normal\">Coverage: 94%</span></div>\n          <div class=\"plot\"></div><div class=\"axis-label\">True value</div>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"chart\">\n          <div class=\"chart-title\">Gene tree frequency<br><span style=\"font-weight:normal\">Coverage: 94%</span></div>\n          <div class=\"plot\"></div><div class=\"axis-label\">True value</div>\n        </div>\n\n        <div class=\"chart\">\n          <div class=\"chart-title\">Effective population size<br><span style=\"font-weight:normal\">Coverage: 92%</span></div>\n          <div class=\"plot\"></div><div class=\"axis-label\">True value</div>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"chart\">\n          <div class=\"chart-title\">Mean effective population size<br><span style=\"font-weight:normal\">Coverage: 95%</span></div>\n          <div class=\"plot\"></div><div class=\"axis-label\">True value</div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n\n      <p class=\"results-note\">Well-calibrated simulation study analysing nS = 16 species, nG = 48 taxa, and k = 50 genes. One hundred simulations were performed to recover the coverage between “true” simulated values and their estimates under the posterior distribution. Vertical lines represent 95% highest posterior density (HPD) intervals of parameters. Each line represents a single simulation and is colored blue when the true value was contained within the 95% interval, or red otherwise. The top of each plot shows the coverage of each parameter (i.e., the number of MCMC simulations for which the “true” parameter value was contained within the 95% HPD). This result was coherent when we tested 100 and 200 genes, respectively.</p>\n\n      <h2 class=\"section-title conclusion\">Conclusion</h2>\n      <p class=\"conclusion-text\">Our results show all coverage observed is in the expected range, from 90 to 99 inclusive, suggesting the correct implementation of StarBeast3 for all experiments performed. Furthermore, these experiments evidence that startbeast3 is suitable for multispecies coalescent inference on large datasets (100+ genes).</p>\n\n      <footer class=\"footer\">\n        <div class=\"footer-text\">\n          <p><strong>Software Availability:</strong> StarBeast3 is available as an open-source BEAST 2 package with an easy-to-use graphical user interface. Instructions for downloading and running StarBeast3 can be found at https://github.com/rbouckaert/starbeast3</p>\n          <p><strong>Acknowledgments:</strong> The study was supported by a Marsden grant 18-UOA-096 from the Royal Society of New Zealand. Software packages were benchmarked using the New Zealand Science Infrastructure (NeSI) cluster, funded by New Zealand Ministry of Business, Innovation, and Employment.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div>\n          <div class=\"qr-title\">StarBeast3<br>preprint:</div>\n          <div class=\"qr placeholder\" aria-label=\"[QR code: StarBeast3 preprint]\"></div>\n        </div>\n      </footer>\n    </section>\n  </div>\n</main>\n</body>\n</html>"
      },
      "finish_reason": "stop"
    }
